      "reviewList": [
        {
          "additionText": "",
          "age": "1981",
          "atopy": false,
          "badText": "There's no difference in terms of a reduction in fine lines or wrinkles however I wasn't really expecting to see results within 3 short weeks. It's going to take a load of patience, maybe some sprinkles of faith and consistency for something like this to work its magic.",
          "blind": 0,
          "brand": "티암 (TIAM)",
          "commentCount": 0,
          "encryptedProductId": "56d0bb93e178d13adf21693e6e12f15d",
          "gender": "여성",
          "goodText": "The anti-aging moisturizer not only boasts a new look but new formula to woo those chasing radiant and younger looking skin. Said to be more mild than its previous version, the formulation underwent improvement to deliver skin effectiveness without the burden of irritation. It features the weakest retinoid, Retinyl Palmitate which works in conjunction with Fish Collagen to give skin a youthful appearance and firmness.\n\nI was onboard with this for a couple of reasons, firstly Retinol legit scares me, so I found comfort in its still effective but less intimidating kin, Retinyl Palmitate. Secondly I'm always keen on having anti-aging products in my skincare regimen. Despite its promises to be gentle, I still thought it was necessary to gradually work this into my routine instead of making it a daily thing from the get-go. I did experience a minor breakout and some itching that lasted a couple of days around week 2 but as someone who is always testing products, I honestly can't tell which product is to blame so I'm not going to point any fingers here.\n\nThe Vita A Anti-Wrinkle Moisturizer has a super elegant, lightweight texture that spreads easily and sinks in quickly giving skin a finish that is free of tackiness/greasiness. It does however encourage a ton of grease within an hour or two of application. The product gives my oily skin ample moisturization but I'm not sure if it's occlusive enough for those with dry skin. While Tia’m did away with unpleasant fragrance, there is a hint of citrus here that fades shortly after application.\n\n\n\n",
